        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "media": {
            "duration": 8997,
            "fileSize": 145852632
          },
          "author": "Lemony Snicket",
          "description": "In the tradition of great storytellers, from Dickens to Dahl, comes an exquisitely dark comedy that is both literary and irreverent, hilarious and deftly crafted. Never before has a tale of three likeable and unfortunate children been quite so enchanting, or quite so uproariously unhappy.\n\nAre you made fainthearted by death? Does fire unnerve you? Is a villain something that might crop up in future nightmares of yours? Are you thrilled by nefarious plots? Is cold porridge upsetting to you? Vicious threats? Hooks? Uncomfortable clothing?It is likely that your answers will reveal A Series of Unfortunate Events to be ill-suited for your personal use. A librarian, bookseller, or acquaintance should be able to suggest books more appropriate for your fragile temperament. But to the rarest of readers we say, \"Proceed, but cautiously.\"",
          "audioPreviewUrl": "https://audio-previews-media.api.yotoplay.com/audio-previews/6cf89344938084f1b92219093d02902dd188ec2aaf672f74a5a482d7c8844d80/xSWCOwbngI-ZL-1TgJAzyFzHpjHZAXJq6JxxIoftFkA.mp3",
